&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nova Credit is the industry’s leading cash flow intelligence platform, enabling businesses to unlock the power of cash flow data in how they operate. The company leverages its industry-leading data infrastructure, innovative intelligence layer, &amp;amp; robust FCRA-compliance to boost approvals, improve offers, fight fraud, drive responsible growth, and more. Nova Credit supports over 7,000 businesses including organizations such as Chase, HSBC, SoFi, Sallie Mae, Appfolio, and Yardi, with a growing suite of products. Nova Credit is proud to be backed by an exceptional group of investors and was named in Forbes’ Fintech 50 in 2025 and Built In’s Best Places to Work, 2025.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nova Credit’s solutions are among the most widely used in multifamily. They’re embedded in four of the top five property management software platforms and used by more than 7,000 property management companies. Our Rental Housing platform helps operators verify income, determine eligibility, and assess risk using bank, payroll, and document data that traditional screening misses, so they can approve more qualified renters and lease units faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Director of Growth Marketing, you’ll own brand and demand across our Rental Housing platform. Your most important challenge is creating the market for cash flow underwriting: we want every leasing director, regional manager, and asset manager to know Nova Credit and why it matters to their portfolio. Operators who have access to our products through their software should use them, and operators who don’t should ask for them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect about three-quarters of your focus to go to Nova-owned programs and a quarter to co-marketing with our platform partners. You’ll report to our Head of Rental Housing, partner with a growth team that spans partner enablement, events, and product marketing, and work closely with our account management and new business teams. This is a hands-on individual contributor role to start, with the opportunity to build a team as the program proves itself.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(224, 62, 45);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a hybrid full-time role (3 days per week in office on Mondays, Tuesdays, and Thursdays) based in the New York Metropolitan area.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU’LL DO:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the strategy to take cash flow underwriting from unknown to in demand. Define the problem in the industry’s own language: the qualified renters, vacancy days, and risk that credit-only screening costs operators and owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop ideas for original research and flagship content, often built on Nova’s proprietary renter cash flow data. Partner with product marketing to produce them, and own the campaigns that make each one a reference point for the industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with account management and new business to recruit early-adopter operators, and turn their results into stories and proof points that make the category credible.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run campaigns across our full platform, from income verification to eligibility determination and cash flow underwriting, and build Nova’s reputation in industry media and PR as the authority on fair, compliant screening.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow a clean, compliant, well-segmented database of property management decision-makers, and engage it through email, newsletters, and nurture programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run high-reach programs with industry media and associations. Set our rental housing event strategy, including which events we attend and what we focus on there, with our events partner leading execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build account-based programs for high-value operators and institutional portfolios, including REITs and PE-backed owners, making the case that screening policy drives NOI, risk, and asset value. Create demand on platforms where Nova isn’t yet available.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Co-market with our software partners through co-branded research, joint webinars, and campaigns that reach their customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Close the loop on every program. Plan follow-up before launch, personally follow up with interested decision-makers alongside the Head of Rental Housing, and report results from awareness through adoption and revenue. Set goals and manage budget.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST 90 DAYS, YOU’LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn our products, partners, customers, and market, and audit our existing contacts, content, events, and past programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a quick win using existing assets, such as a campaign built on our published cash flow research.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present a 12-month plan, including our event calendar, with clear goals for awareness, demand, database growth, and adoption.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST YEAR, YOU’LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run Nova’s owned channels on a consistent cadence with regular reporting, and measurably grow our database and demand for our products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help bring our first early-adopter operators live on cash flow underwriting and publish their results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make cash flow underwriting a recognized idea among property management decision-makers, with Nova Credit as the name associated with it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate demand both on platforms where our products are available and on platforms where they aren’t yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR SKILLSET:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years in B2B marketing, with significant experience in property management, proptech, multifamily, or rental housing. Industry fluency is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proven track record of creating a market for a new product or category. You’ve made customers want something they didn’t know they needed. This is the most important skill for this role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building a marketable database and consistently running owned programs (email, content, sponsored programs, events) with measurable results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discipline about follow-through. A program isn’t finished until leads are worked and results are reported.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An existing network across operators, software platforms, industry media, and associations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong storytelling and campaign instincts. You know which ideas will get the industry’s attention and how to turn data-driven content into campaigns people read and share.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience co-marketing with partners in markets where customers buy through platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hands-on builder who is comfortable as the first dedicated marketer in a fast-moving business and ties marketing to adoption and revenue.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;$195,000 - $222,300 USD per year&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The above compensation range is for U.S.-based candidates and is dependent on individual experience, skills, education, location, and qualifications. We consider all elements of compensation as a part of the value we provide to Novans. This may include base salary, equity grants, incentive compensation for eligible roles, professional development, flexible PTO, and tenure rewards. We offer U.S.-based Novans competitive, employer-subsidized medical, dental, and vision plans, in addition to mental health and wellness benefits and a range of other benefits and perks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer where everyone is welcome at Nova Credit. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected class, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We encourage all qualified candidates, including those with a criminal history, to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Before submitting your application, please review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.novacredit.com/applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; to learn how we collect, use, and protect your personal information during the application process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nova Credit is a credit infrastructure and analytics company that enables businesses to grow responsibly by harnessing alternative credit data. The company leverages its unique data infrastructure, industry-leading analytics &amp;amp; FCRA-compliance to help lenders fill in the gaps that exist in traditional credit analytics. Nova Credit provides access to the fragmented universe of consumer financial data and transforms it into compliant, actionable risk analytics through a suite of solutions designed to increase conversion through expanded coverage, speed, and reliability. Nova Credit supports over 7,000 businesses including organizations such as HSBC, SoFi, Scotiabank, AppFolio, and Yardi, who work with Nova Credit to make smarter credit decisions through cash flow underwriting with Cash Atlas™, quickly and accurately verify income with Income Navigator, verify income and assets with Eligibility Compass, and reach new-to-country consumers with Credit Passport®. We were named in &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/fintech50/&quot;&gt;Forbes’ Fintech 50&lt;/a&gt; in 2025 and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.novacredit.com/corporate-blog/built-in-honors-nova-credit-in-its-esteemed-2025-best-places-to-work-awards&quot;&gt;Built In’s Best Places to Work, 2025&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Nova Credit’s Information Security Lead, you will be a hands-on, all-rounder security practitioner at the heart of our InfoSec function. You will partner closely with the Director of Information Security to mature our security program, moving fluidly between deep-in-the-weeds technical work (configuring tooling, hardening systems, investigating alerts, automating controls) and the Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC) work that earns us the trust of some of the world’s largest financial institutions (responding to customer security questionnaires, supporting SOC 2 and ISO 27001 audits, executing on our control sets, and running third-party risk reviews).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is built for someone who is happy doing both. You bring an engineer’s instinct for solving security problems with configuration, and the practitioner’s patience for the questionnaire and audit work that proves out our controls. You will work cross-functionally with the rest of the company, while you will own meaningful technical and program-level initiatives from your first quarter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(224, 62, 45);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a hybrid role (3 days per week in office on Mondays, Tuesdays, and Thursdays) based in the New York City Metropolitan area.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST MONTH, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop a working understanding of Nova Credit’s products, our AWS-based infrastructure, and the data flows that matter most from a security perspective.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarize yourself with our control sets, frameworks, and policies (SOC 2 Type II, ISO 27001, internal standards) and our existing inventory of customer-facing security commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Get hands-on with our security tooling stack, EDR, MDM, SSO/IAM, DLP, cloud security posture management, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shadow incoming customer security questionnaires and due diligence reviews to learn the cadence, the source-of-truth artifacts, and our standard responses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pick up your first hands-on tickets, things like endpoint hardening, MDM tuning, IAM cleanup, or evidence collection, to build operational muscle memory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet your stakeholders across the rest of the company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST QUARTER, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Start to own customer security questionnaires and due diligence reviews end-to-end, from intake, to evidence pulls, to clean responses, to the follow-up calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure, tune, and operate security tooling across our stack (EDR, MDM, SSO/IAM, DLP, Google Workspace settings).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Triage and respond to security alerts, bug bounty reports, and internal escalations; document repeatable response runbooks for what you handle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to third-party risk reviews of new vendors and re-reviews of existing critical suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Surface and propose fixes for at least one process gap or control weakness you identify during onboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST YEAR, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own an agreed-on slice of Nova Credit’s security program end-to-end,&amp;nbsp; e.g., IAM/SSO, endpoint and MDM, vulnerability management, customer-trust/questionnaire program, or third-party risk, with clear, measurable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own customer security questionnaires and due diligence reviews end-to-end, from intake to evidence pulls, to clean responses, and attending follow-up calls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive at least one significant hardening or modernization initiative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a go-to internal expert for technical security questions from Engineering, Product and Data Science&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the Director of Information Security on roadmap, prioritization, and how our Information Security program scales as Nova grows&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR SKILLSET:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 3–6+ years across information security, security engineering, cloud security, or technical GRC roles, ideally with at least some time in a high-growth fintech, financial services, or regulated SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on technical depth&lt;/strong&gt;: Comfortable configuring and operating modern security tooling such asEDR, MDM, SSO/IAM, DLP, and cloud security tooling. Knowledge of Jamf, SentinelOne, Okta are a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cloud security&lt;/strong&gt;: Working knowledge of AWS security, IAM, networking, KMS, logging, and common misconfiguration risks. You can reason about real architecture and point out where the risks are.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Foundational concepts&lt;/strong&gt;: Solid grasp of networking, identity, cryptography, secure SDLC, and web application security. You don’t need to be an offensive security specialist, but you should know how attackers think.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GRC / audit fluency&lt;/strong&gt;: Direct experience with SOC 2 Type II and ISO 27001 are a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication&lt;/strong&gt;: You can explain a technical risk to engineering team members, write a clean policy, and disagree productively with an Engineering lead in the same week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;All-rounder mindset&lt;/strong&gt;: You are equally willing to dig into a misconfigured IAM policy and fill out a 200-question bank questionnaire. You don’t silo the work into “technical” and “non-technical.”&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$118,400 - 140,600 USD per year&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The above compensation range is for United States-based candidates and is dependent on individual experience, skills, education, location, and qualifications. We consider all elements of compensation to be a part of the value we provide to Novans. This may include base salary, equity grants, incentive compensation for eligible roles, professional development, flexible PTO, and tenure rewards.&amp;nbsp; In the U.S., our benefits package includes comprehensive and generously subsidized medical, dental, and vision insurance options, along with a company-sponsored 401k plan, parental leave of absence, sick time off, and paid time off vacation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Everyone is welcome at Nova Credit. We are an equal-opportunity employer where diversity and inclusion are central pillars of our company strategy. We seek applicants who understand, embrace, and thrive in a multicultural and globalized world. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected class, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We encourage all qualified candidates, including those with a criminal history, to apply.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Before submitting your application, please review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.novacredit.com/applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; to learn how we collect, use, and protect your personal information during the application process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Nova Credit is the industry’s leading cash flow intelligence platform, enabling businesses to unlock the power of cash flow data in how they operate. The company leverages its industry-leading data infrastructure, innovative intelligence layer, and robust FCRA-compliance to boost approvals, improve offers, fight fraud, drive responsible growth, and more. Nova Credit supports over 7,000 businesses including organizations such as Chase, HSBC, SoFi, Sallie Mae, Appfolio, and Yardi, with a growing suite of products. Nova Credit is proud to be backed by an exceptional group of investors and was named in &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/fintech50/&quot;&gt;Forbes’ Fintech 50&lt;/a&gt; in 2025 and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.novacredit.com/corporate-blog/built-in-honors-nova-credit-in-its-esteemed-2025-best-places-to-work-awards&quot;&gt;Built In’s Best Places to Work, 2025&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nova Credit is looking for a Senior Deployment Lead to implement Nova Credit&#39;s suite of products—Credit Passport®, Cash Atlas™, and Income Navigator—with new and existing customers post-sale. Your work will directly impact our global revenue growth and advance our mission to power a more fair and inclusive financial system for the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Success in this role requires strong project management skills and the ability to coordinate with technical and business stakeholders. Drawing on our experience with past enterprise-scale deployments, you&#39;ll ensure deployments meet and exceed client expectations. You&#39;ll work across client organizations—from technology teams to marketing and credit risk policy stakeholders—to drive successful product deployment and integration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Internally, you&#39;ll orchestrate cross-functional collaboration to deliver deployments that are on time, on-scope, and positioned for revenue growth. The ideal candidate thrives in a fast-paced environment with some operational ambiguity, can manage multiple complex deployments simultaneously, and excels at stakeholder management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(224, 62, 45);&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;This is a hybrid role (3 days per week in office on Mondays, Tuesdays, and Thursdays) based in the New York City Metropolitan area reporting to the Head of Solutions.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST MONTH, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understand Nova Credit’s value, business model, and products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build relationships within your portfolio of enterprise accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST QUARTER, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master our product technology, including the basics of enabling technical integration, user experience, customer acquisition, and credit risk decisioning&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with customer business teams to shape business objectives and integration requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and execute deployments at Nova Credit’s strategic accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Measure and report on the ongoing effectiveness of respective customer launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate key pre- and post-launch touchpoints with an Executive level stakeholder audience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strategic growth plans, that enable our leadership team to interact with key prospects and grow an account’s overall potential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WITHIN THE FIRST YEAR, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Successfully deploy Nova Credit’s solutions to multiple enterprise clients&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be directly responsible for driving significant revenue realization via on-time and on-value deployments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Nova Credit’s Solution Architects, Account Managers, Product Managers, and Engineering teams - among others - to strategically influence product priorities, and further improve Nova Credit’s core product features&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR SKILLSET:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years experience as a Deployment Lead, Client Solutions/Customer Success Manager, Engagement Manager, Technical Project Manager, Professional Services Lead, or Management Consultant. Past experience working with clients in the financial services industry is a plus.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical implementation experience - you can configure a customer environment, and explain technical concepts to business stakeholders (API, Webhook, etc). Additionally, we’ll teach you about Nova Credit’s products, but our customers and products are inherently technical and you should have the curiosity to learn and creatively problem solve&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entrepreneurial mindset - Adaptable to hybrid work settings, and resourceful in a fast-paced, lean environment (wearing multiple hats)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of autonomy in delivering multi-stakeholder initiatives - Ability to take full ownership of your account portfolio and make key decisions to deliver ambitious business outcomes. This includes: deciding when to include our executive team in customer escalations; defining de-escalation plans;&amp;nbsp; mobilizing cross-functional teams to solution customer requests; and executing a mix of high versus mid-touch engagement commensurate with the growth potential of your customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base Salary Range: $153,600 - $182,400 USD&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The above compensation range is for U.S.-based candidates and is dependent on individual experience, skills, education, location, and qualifications. We consider all elements of compensation as a part of the value we provide to Novans. This may include base salary, equity grants, incentive compensation for eligible roles, professional development, flexible PTO, and tenure rewards. We offer U.S.-based Novans competitive, employer-subsidized medical, dental, and vision plans, in addition to mental health and wellness benefits and a range of other benefits and perks.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are an equal-opportunity employer where everyone is welcome at Nova Credit. We do not discriminate on the basis of any protected class, including race, religion, color, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, or disability status. We encourage all qualified candidates, including those with a criminal history, to apply.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;h3 style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;Before submitting your application, please review our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.novacredit.com/applicant-privacy-notice&quot;&gt;Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt; to learn how we collect, use, and protect your personal information during the application process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;section page-centered&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHO WE ARE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nova Credit is the industry’s leading cash flow intelligence platform, enabling businesses to unlock the power of cash flow data in how they operate. The company leverages its industry-leading data infrastructure, innovative intelligence layer, &amp;amp; robust FCRA-compliance to boost approvals, improve offers, fight fraud, drive responsible growth, and more. Nova Credit supports over 7,000 businesses including organizations such as Chase, HSBC, SoFi, Sallie Mae, Appfolio, and Yardi, with a growing suite of products. Nova Credit is proud to be backed by an exceptional group of investors and was named in &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.forbes.com/lists/fintech50/&quot;&gt;Forbes’ Fintech 50&lt;/a&gt; in 2025 and &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.novacredit.com/corporate-blog/built-in-honors-nova-credit-in-its-esteemed-2025-best-places-to-work-awards&quot;&gt;Built In’s Best Places to Work, 2025&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us to help unlock economic opportunities for consumers historically excluded from traditional credit systems. We foster a dynamic, inclusive environment that values diversity, intellectual honesty, and innovation, committed to supporting your professional growth. &lt;strong&gt;For more on our engineering culture, check out our recent &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.novacredit.com/corporate-blog/engineering-at-nova-credit&quot;&gt;blog post&lt;/a&gt;!&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;OUR TECHNOLOGY STACK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We leverage Node.js, React, TypeScript, Python, PostgreSQL, and AWS to bring our products to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE OPPORTUNITY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to lead key technical projects from design to delivery, drive the implementation of scalable and robust solutions across our products, and contribute to our technical roadmap while mentoring junior engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR PROFILE &amp;amp; EXPERTISE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of relevant experience, ideally in high-growth or early-stage startups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong expertise in modern software technologies, with ability to quickly learn and ramp into our tech stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive problem-solver with a demonstrated ability to independently navigate and resolve complex technical challenges in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaborator and communicator, effectively bridging gaps between technical teams and non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR CONTRIBUTIONS ACROSS A RANGE OF PROJECTS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing and building enterprise-grade APIs and platform-level features (web and mobile).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leading the implementation and launch of new integrations with key data suppliers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and productizing advanced data models to effectively deploy new attributes and scores.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advancing architectural enhancements to support new product use cases and ensure platform scalability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IN THE FIRST MONTH, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Land your “new hire” ticket in the first week, and contribute to at least one key roadmap feature in the first month.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarize yourself with our software development lifecycle and technical strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Quickly grasp our business model, product offerings, and customer value proposition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate seamlessly with the team, understanding our working style, mission, and values.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;IN THE FIRST QUARTER, YOU&#39;LL:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead significant technical initiatives, taking end-to-end ownership from design through delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently participate and make impactful contributions across team norms (e.g., project planning, thorough code reviews, QA, on-call rotation).&lt;/li&gt;
